body: "## Summary\n`context next` accepts inherited context projection/depth flags but neither applies nor validates them. Invalid controls return success and a normal recommendation.\n\nReproduced with the official installed `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.9.30 on Linux, using disposable synthetic non-Git trackers. No implementation changes are included in this issue.\n\n## Reproduction\n```bash\nLAB=$(mktemp -d)\nmkdir -p \"$LAB/home\" \"$LAB/work\"\nexport HOME=\"$LAB/home\" PM_PATH=\"$LAB/work/.agents/pm\"\nexport PM_GLOBAL_PATH=\"$LAB/global\" PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1\ncd \"$LAB/work\"\npm init \"$PM_PATH\" --defaults --author audit --agent-guidance skip --json >/dev/null\npm create task \"Audit sample\" --id t1 --description \"Execution detail\" --json >/dev/null\n```\n```bash\npm context next --json\npm context next --fields id,title,description --json\npm context next --fields notafield --json\npm context next --depth nonsense --json\n```\n\n## Actual\nAll commands exit 0. The same recommendation shape is returned: 17 fields, including fields not requested by the explicit projection, while the stored description remains absent. An unknown projection and a nonsensical depth receive no typed error or ignored-option warning.\n\n## Expected and impact\nA supported option must be applied and validated. If a parent option has no meaning on a child command, reject it with a typed actionable error before executing the command. Silent acceptance teaches agents an incorrect contract and can withhold explicitly requested execution detail.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Inventory parent/global option inheritance versus child handlers and declared flag contracts.\n2. Define supported projection/depth semantics for next; reuse the shared projection validator and renderer where appropriate.\n3. Explicitly reject unsupported inherited controls rather than silently swallowing them.\n4. Generate help/contract applicability from the same registry used by dispatch validation.\n5. Add parent-flags × subcommands tests, with representative valid and invalid values, and CLI/MCP parity for supported features.\n\n## Regression acceptance\n- [ ] An id/title/description projection returns the requested stored description and documented mandatory metadata, or is explicitly rejected as unsupported\n- [ ] Unknown fields and invalid depth return nonzero typed errors\n- [ ] Parent flag placement and aliases do not change validation\n- [ ] Recommended and companion rows follow one documented projection rule\n- [ ] Tests cover other inherited controls to catch accepted-but-unused flags\n- [ ] No regression to next ranking, blocker visibility or token-budget enforcement\n\n## Ownership and duplicate check\nChild of #1363; conformance coverage for #1361/#1362. Closed #440/#156 concerned context projection availability; this is the nested next dispatch path. Closed #1264 concerned token-budget enforcement and is distinct. Searched open and closed context-next, fields and depth issues."
